innovations.description:
La Maison des Enfants Extraordinaires offers therapeutic workshops, holiday camps and private treatment services for children.
The association also supports the parents of these ‘extraordinary’ children through:
Advice and therapeutic guidance;
Parenting support workshops;
Training courses to help them better support their child;
Fun workshops designed to give parents a breather.
Finally, MEEX offers training courses for professionals who work with children with neurodevelopmental disorders on a daily basis (healthcare professionals, teachers, etc.).
Beyond geographical accessibility, the association aims to ensure that its services are accessible to all families, regardless of their budget. Consequently, whilst parents currently contribute 40 per cent of the cost of MEEX’s services, a ‘Coup de pouce’ scheme is available for families experiencing financial difficulties. This scheme, managed by the EDUCADIFF Endowment Fund, is funded by donations from individuals and businesses.

