innovations.description:
The association:
Implements more sustainable waste management through reduction at source and the recovery of food waste;
Supports urban agriculture by improving soil quality and reducing the use of chemical fertilisers through the use of compost;
Contributes to improving air quality by reducing greenhouse gas emissions through the use of bicycles;
Combats climate change by sequestering carbon in the soil through composting;
Promotes local employment and the creation of dedicated roles open to people on integration schemes;
Creates social spaces in the city centred around composting and gardening;
Changes the public’s perception of waste through awareness-raising initiatives.
Sikle has developed a bespoke bicycle-based food waste collection service designed to be simple and efficient, aimed at businesses (hotels, cafés, restaurants, corporate offices, food retailers) and private individuals as part of a partnership with local authorities. All the organic waste collected is recycled through composting, either at sites located in municipal gardens or directly on the land of partner farmers. The compost produced at municipal recycling sites is largely reused on site by gardeners and market gardeners, in return for a nominal fee. The remainder is available for sale at local distribution points or via bicycle delivery.

