innovations.description:
The NGO has created a simple and effective direct support model for vulnerable elderly people. Through the campaign “A loaf of bread a day for a poor elderly person,” the community can quickly contribute with small but regular donations that ensure daily food for seniors. Local volunteers are involved in identifying urgent cases and delivering aid directly to beneficiaries’ homes. We use social media and local partnerships to mobilize people, bakeries, and small businesses to support the cause consistently. The solution focuses on rapid response, transparency, and direct human contact. In this way, elderly people receive not only food, but also attention, moral support, and the feeling that they are not forgotten.
The innovation of the project lies in creating a simple, efficient, and easily replicable community-based model focused on direct and continuous involvement.
The main differentiating factors compared to similar initiatives are:
• daily and continuous intervention, not occasional support;
• direct involvement of the community in supporting each individual case;
• building a local active network of volunteers, bakeries, churches, and local authorities;
• direct identification of beneficiaries through constant human contact;
• extending support beyond food, based on real needs observed in the field.
Through this approach, the project builds direct relationships between community members and vulnerable elderly people, reducing social distance and isolation.

