innovations.evidence:
Salinaria has created an accessible and welcoming community wellbeing space for children, families and adults in a small town environment. The project has contributed to: improving access to wellbeing and preventive health services; creating inclusive and family-friendly community activities; supporting children’s emotional wellbeing through educational and creative activities developed around the SARI concept; promoting environmental awareness, empathy and inclusion of children with disabilities; encouraging social interaction and community involvement in a calm and safe environment.
In the first three months of activity:
26 subscriptions were sold (packages of 5 and 10 sessions);
approximately 30 unique clients benefited from Salinaria's services;
individual sessions were conducted for adults and families;
6 free sessions were provided to community beneficiaries;
approximately 70 children participated in activities organized across 4 groups;
a reading evening was organized with 11 participants;
a drawing competition dedicated to World Water Day was held, receiving 56 entries;
4 SARI educational themes were developed;
approximately 200 educational worksheets were printed, of which around 80 have already been used by children.
Collaborations and partnerships were developed with:
schools and kindergartens;
Lions Club;
Basti Box Sports Association;
the Association of Persons with Disabilities (partnership currently in development). As a social enterprise, Salinaria also contributes to local social impact by reinvesting most of its profit into social and educational initiatives dedicated to vulnerable children and families, including free and subsidized halotherapy sessions for children and people with limited financial resources.

