innovations.raw_text:
Salinaria – Community Wellbeing and Salt Therapy Center
Families and children in small towns often have limited access to affordable wellbeing and preventive health services, as well as to safe and inclusive community spaces focused on relaxation, prevention and quality time together. In Salonta and nearby communities, air pollution, seasonal respiratory discomfort, stress and limited opportunities for healthy community interaction affect both children and adults. At the same time, there are few accessible local spaces dedicated to wellbeing, emotional balance and family-oriented activities.
Salinaria offers an innovative community-based approach that combines modern halotherapy technology, wellbeing, social inclusion and educational activities for children within a calm and accessible environment designed for families and local communities. Unlike traditional wellbeing services focused only on therapy, Salinaria integrates prevention, emotional wellbeing, community interaction and social economy principles into one local initiative. The project creates a welcoming space where children, parents and grandparents can relax, reconnect and participate in creative and community-oriented activities together. A unique element of the project is SARI, the friendly crystal mascot of Salinaria, developed to support children’s emotional wellbeing through stories, educational coloring sheets and interactive activities that encourage creativity, calmness and positive social interaction. Each educational activity also promotes environmental awareness, inclusion of children with disabilities, empathy, community involvement and respect for diversity in a friendly and accessible way.
