innovations.raw_text:
AdoptIDee
As we get older our creativity tends to reduce. Our experiences in life, own motivation and structures we are used to live often have a negative influence on our creativity. Also local entrepreneurs struggle with issues but aren't equipped with the right amount of creativity that could really give an out-of-the-box solution for their problems.That's why we need young people because they are not hampered by these effects and trully have pure ideas.
By offering a six-step approach we connect the local entrepreneur with a class of a local school. Each class adopts one entrepreneur and in groups of 4 to 5 students they work on a solution for the problem of the local entrepreneur. Because the average class consists of approx. 20 children, each entrepreneur receives up to 4 or 5 original solutions. One of the steps within the six-step approach is that the children as well as the teacher will visit the local entrepreneur to introduce the children to the workings of a company in an early age. Also it stimulates the regional coherence.
- regional coherence;
- teachers actively involved with local entrepreneurs and their problems so that the teaching material becomes very up to date;
- local entrepreneurs get insprired;
- children get in contact with their possible future employer

